<h1>Nielsen Media Impact Pricing: Complete 2026 Breakdown</h1>

<p>Nielsen Media Impact is Nielsen's cross-media planning platform for reach, frequency, duplication, and scenario planning across TV, streaming, digital, audio, and other channels. It is used by agencies and enterprise advertisers that need Nielsen-backed planning assumptions.</p>

<p>Pricing is custom and enterprise-oriented. Public monthly plans are not available.</p>

<h2>Pricing Model</h2>

<p>Nielsen Media Impact uses a <strong>custom enterprise licensing model</strong>. Cost can depend on markets, users, modules, audience segments, data access, channel coverage, and whether it is bundled with Nielsen ONE, Scarborough, Commspoint, or other Nielsen tools.</p>

<p>For many buyers, the main value is planning confidence: deduplicated reach, incremental reach, frequency management, and scenario comparison before media dollars are committed.</p>

<h2>Pricing Tiers</h2>

<table>
<thead>
<tr><th>Tier</th><th>Pricing</th><th>Best For</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Core Reach Planning</td><td>Custom quote</td><td>Teams modeling reach and frequency across major channels</td></tr>
<tr><td>Advanced Audiences</td><td>Custom quote</td><td>Teams adding segments, category data, or Scarborough-powered audiences</td></tr>
<tr><td>Enterprise Nielsen Suite</td><td>Custom quote</td><td>Organizations using Media Impact with Nielsen ONE and other Nielsen products</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>

<h2>What's Included</h2>

<p>Packages may include cross-media reach and frequency planning, deduplication, incremental reach analysis, scenario planning, advanced audience segments, and Nielsen data access. Exact scope depends on the negotiated agreement.</p>

<p>Buyers should confirm which channels, markets, audience segments, and export or reporting workflows are included.</p>

<h2>Total Cost of Ownership</h2>

<ul>
<li><strong>Data and market scope:</strong> Broader coverage usually means a larger contract.</li>
<li><strong>Nielsen suite dependencies:</strong> Existing Nielsen measurement or planning agreements can affect packaging.</li>
<li><strong>Planning governance:</strong> Teams need agreement on reach, frequency, audience, and channel assumptions.</li>
<li><strong>Training:</strong> Planners and research teams need onboarding to interpret scenario outputs consistently.</li>
<li><strong>Workflow integration:</strong> Confirm how plans move into buying systems and client-facing deliverables.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Who It's Best For / Not For</h2>

<p><strong>Best for:</strong> Agencies and enterprise advertisers that need Nielsen-backed cross-media reach and frequency planning.</p>

<p><strong>Not ideal for:</strong> Teams looking for a tactical media buying tool, a lightweight plan builder, or a self-serve dashboard with public pricing.</p>

